@startuml seller-receiving-money-flow
!define STRIPE_COLOR #FFE082
!define BACKEND_COLOR #E1F5FF
!define BANK_COLOR #C8E6C9

' Seller's-eye view of where money goes and when.
' Manual-capture + destination-charge, Stripe Thailand.

start
:Buyer authorizes payment\n(no money has moved yet);

:Payment.status = REQUIRES_CAPTURE\nListing.status = PAID;

if (Seller delivers item at pickup?) then (Yes)
  :Buyer taps "Confirm Receipt";
  :Backend calls\nstripe.paymentIntents.capture();
else (No / dispute / no-show)
  if (Within ~6 days?) then (Yes)
    :Buyer or admin cancels PI\n→ Listing back to AVAILABLE\n→ Seller earns nothing;
    stop
  else (No)
    :Auth expires (Stripe ~7d cap)\n→ Auto-canceled\n→ Listing back to AVAILABLE;
    stop
  endif
endif

:Stripe routes funds in one capture:
  amount        debited from buyer
  platformFee   → platform Stripe balance
  sellerNet     → seller's connected-account balance
(no separate transfer call needed);

:Payment.status = SUCCEEDED\nListing.status = RECEIVED\nSellerProfile.totalEarnedSatang += sellerNet;

:Funds sit in seller's Stripe\nconnected-account balance;

note right
  This is "pending" from the seller's POV
  but it is tracked by STRIPE, not by our DB.
  We never store pending/available locally.
end note

:Wait for Stripe's payout schedule\n(Thailand default: rolling T+7 business days, THB);

:Stripe initiates payout\nto seller's Thai bank\nautomatically;

:Webhook: payout.paid\n→ totalPaidOutSatang += amount\n→ push notification to seller;

:Seller sees deposit in their Thai bank account;
stop

note right
  Key truths:
  - Stripe owns the rails, the schedule, AND the balance.
  - Our DB only stores: Stripe IDs, statuses, lifetime totals.
  - For "how much can I withdraw?" → call
      stripe.balance.retrieve({ stripeAccount }).
  - For "show my past payouts" → call
      stripe.payouts.list({ stripeAccount }).
  - Thailand restriction: THB-only payouts to TH banks.
end note

@enduml
